# Accepted-risk CVEs for the CD pipeline's Trivy scan (.github/workflows/cd.yml).
# Empty by default — this pipeline has never run against a real image build,
# so there is nothing here yet to justify ignoring. Add entries only after a
# real CI run surfaces a CVE that's genuinely not exploitable in this app's
# context, one per line, with a reason and a recheck date so entries don't
# silently go stale:
#
# CVE-2024-XXXXX exp:2026-06-01
# # Reason: <why this doesn't apply here — e.g. unused code path, patched
# # upstream with no release yet, mitigated by network policy>

# --- backend image (python:3.12.12-slim / debian 13.3), first real scan
# 2026-09-28. All entries below are Debian-unfixed ("affected") OS-package
# CVEs in tools the container never exercises: it runs a single uvicorn
# process as non-root `app` behind the ALB+WAF — no logins, no suid mount
# helpers, no systemd, no ncurses/perl runtime. Recheck after the next
# python:3.12.x-slim base bump.

CVE-2026-76642 exp:2026-10-28
# util-linux family (bsdutils, libmount1, mount, login, ...): external mount
# helper handling. Container performs no mounts; binaries unused.
CVE-2026-78408 exp:2026-10-28
# util-linux nsenter --join-cgroup root leak. Container joins no cgroups;
# nsenter unused.
CVE-2026-78409 exp:2026-10-28
# util-linux X-mount.subdir detached-tree mount issue. No mounts performed.
CVE-2026-78410 exp:2026-10-28
# util-linux restricted bind-mount pinning. No mounts performed.
CVE-2026-12064 exp:2026-10-28
# curl/libcurl SSH host-verification bypass. curl only runs the container
# HEALTHCHECK against http://localhost:8000/health — no SSH, no remote URLs.
CVE-2026-8286 exp:2026-10-28
# curl insecure connection establishment (TLS). Same localhost-only use.
CVE-2026-8458 exp:2026-10-28
# libcurl unauthorized connection reuse. Same localhost-only use.
CVE-2026-8927 exp:2026-10-28
# curl uncleared proxy credential disclosure. No proxy configured in image.
CVE-2025-69720 exp:2026-10-28
# ncurses buffer overflow (libncursesw6, libtinfo6, ncurses-base). ncurses is
# not used by the app; present only as a debian base transitive dep.
CVE-2026-16742 exp:2026-10-28
# systemd-homed local privilege escalation (libsystemd0, libudev1). systemd
# does not run inside the container.
CVE-2026-9538 exp:2026-10-28
# perl-Archive-Tar DoS (perl-base). No perl code executes in the image;
# perl-base ships with the debian base.
CVE-2026-54369 exp:2026-10-28
# libacl symlink traversal privilege escalation. ACL tooling unused; app
# reads/writes only within its non-root container filesystem.

# --- keycloak image (quay.io/keycloak/keycloak:26.7.4, newest 26.x — no
# patched release exists yet), first real scan 2026-09-28. Vendor-bundled
# jars we cannot bump without forking the image. Keycloak serves plain HTTP
# behind the ALB (TLS terminates there) and is not publicly reachable except
# through the WAF-fronted auth hostname.

CVE-2026-75595 exp:2026-10-28
# io.netty:netty-handler SNI routing bypass. Keycloak's own TLS listener is
# not exposed — ALB terminates TLS and forwards HTTP inside the cluster.
CVE-2026-84939 exp:2026-10-28
# freemarker path traversal. Exploitation requires supplying crafted theme
# templates — admin-realm-only capability, not user-reachable.
CVE-2025-59250 exp:2026-10-28
# mssql-jdbc improper input validation. Keycloak connects to Postgres only;
# the SQL Server JDBC driver is bundled but never loaded.
CVE-2026-13506 exp:2026-10-28
# bcprov-jdk18on denial of service. Requires feeding crafted cert/signature
# input through Keycloak's crypto paths.
CVE-2026-8763 exp:2026-10-28
# bcprov-jdk18on additional DoS vector. Same reasoning as CVE-2026-13506.
CVE-2026-86145 exp:2026-10-28
# pcre2 out-of-bounds write (RHEL9 system lib, will_not_fix). Keycloak does
# not route user input through pcre2 bindings.
CVE-2026-89161 exp:2026-10-28
# pcre2 memory corruption. Same reasoning as CVE-2026-86145.
